. *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
. * Example 1: Revisiting Okun's Law
. *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
. 
. * Download unemployment and real GDP data
. gmd unemp rGDP, version(2025_09)
Global Macro Database by Müller et al. (2025)
Website: https://www.globalmacrodata.com

When using these data, please cite:
[BibTeX code]  [APA-style citation]

When using the gmd Stata command, please further cite:
[BibTeX code]  [APA-style citation]

To save the data locally for faster reloading, use: gmd, fast(yes)
Final dataset: 23574 observations for 2 variables
Version: 2025_09

. 
. * Set panel structure
. xtset id year

Panel variable: id (unbalanced)
 Time variable: year, 1270 to 2030
         Delta: 1 unit

. 
. * Calculate real GDP growth rate
. gen rGDP_gr = (rGDP - L.rGDP) / L.rGDP
(1,045 missing values generated)

. 
. * Visualize Okun's Law relationship
. binsreg unemp rGDP_gr if rGDP_gr < 0.1 & rGDP_gr > -0.1, ///
>     xtitle("Real GDP Growth") ///
>     ytitle("Unemployment") ///
>     scheme(sj)
