. *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
. * Example 2: Two Eras of Money and Inflation
. *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
. 
. * Download money supply and inflation data
. gmd M2 infl, version(2025_09)
Global Macro Database by Müller et al. (2025)
Website: https://www.globalmacrodata.com

When using these data, please cite:
[BibTeX code]  [APA-style citation]

When using the gmd Stata command, please further cite:
[BibTeX code]  [APA-style citation]

To save the data locally for faster reloading, use: gmd, fast(yes)
Final dataset: 27636 observations for 2 variables
Version: 2025_09

. 
. * Set panel structure
. xtset id year

Panel variable: id (unbalanced)
 Time variable: year, 1210 to 2030
         Delta: 1 unit

. 
. * Calculate M2 growth rate
. gen M2_gr = 100 * ((M2 - L.M2) / L.M2)
(18,407 missing values generated)

. 
. * Winsorize at 1st and 99th percentiles
. winsor2 infl M2_gr, cut(1 99) replace trim

. 
. * Pre-1963 era: Strong money-inflation link
. xtreg infl M2_gr if year < 1963, fe cluster(id)

